          "message": {
            "text": "No decorating-box x or phase is propagated. Blink uses the ancestor only for decoration metrics, zoom, and block-axis offset; horizontal wave phase belongs to each painted fragment's DecorationGeometry line origin, so adding ancestor phase state would be incorrect across splits.",
            "markdown": "No decorating-box x or phase is propagated. Blink uses the ancestor only for decoration metrics, zoom, and block-axis offset; horizontal wave phase belongs to each painted fragment's DecorationGeometry line origin, so adding ancestor phase state would be incorrect across splits."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/tree-ops/decoration-propagation.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 44,
                  "endLine": 54,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": " * Wavy phase is deliberately NOT propagated from the decorating box. Blink's\n * `TextDecorationInfo` uses the decorating box only for used font, zoom, and\n * block-axis `offset_from_decorating_box`; `DecorationLinePainter` receives\n * each painted fragment's own `DecorationGeometry::line.origin`. `MakeWave`\n * supplies phase `-wavelength`, and the repeating tile is placed at that line\n * origin, so modulo one wavelength its visible phase is zero at every fragment\n * origin. The renderer therefore anchors at the physical segment x and carries\n * no ancestor phase field here. Skip-ink clips that one wave after construction.\n *\n * DM-1732: each entry also records the decorating element's own measured\n * text baselines (`baselines`), so a `vertical-align`-shifted child (sub/"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
